{"book":{"id":"book-the-third-rainbow-girl-the-long-life-of-a-double-murder-in-appalachia-emma-copley-eisenberg","slug":"the-third-rainbow-girl-the-long-life-of-a-double-murder-in-appalachia-emma-copley-eisenberg","title":"The Third Rainbow Girl: The Long Life of a Double Murder in Appalachia","authors":[{"id":"person-emma-copley-eisenberg","name":"Emma Copley Eisenberg"}],"publisherId":"publisher-hachette-book-group-hachette-books","isbn13":["9780316449212"],"subjects":["True Crime & Justice"],"topics":["Class, Poverty & Inequality","Crime, Policing & Violence","Grief, Trauma & Recovery","Media, Journalism & Public Opinion"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=The%20Third%20Rainbow%20Girl%3A%20The%20Long%20Life%20of%20a%20Double%20Murder%20in%20Appalachia%20Emma%20Copley%20Eisenberg","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=The%20Third%20Rainbow%20Girl%3A%20The%20Long%20Life%20of%20a%20Double%20Murder%20in%20Appalachia%20Emma%20Copley%20Eisenberg","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=The%20Third%20Rainbow%20Girl%3A%20The%20Long%20Life%20of%20a%20Double%20Murder%20in%20Appalachia%20Emma%20Copley%20Eisenberg","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=The%20Third%20Rainbow%20Girl%3A%20The%20Long%20Life%20of%20a%20Double%20Murder%20in%20Appalachia%20Emma%20Copley%20Eisenberg","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL20639891W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-edgar-best-fact-crime-edgar-awards-official-best-fact-crime-database","source-open-library-the-third-rainbow-girl-the-long-life-of-a-double-murder-in-appalachia-emma-copley-eisenberg","source-open-library-summary-the-third-rainbow-girl-the-long-life-of-a-double-murder-in-appalachia-emma-copley-eisenberg"],"publicationYear":2020,"thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/10395468-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0.154,"accessibilityScore":0.022,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[{"id":"character_driven","score":0.22,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"life of\""]},{"id":"narrative","score":0.18,"confidence":"low","evidence":["catalog text contains \"murder\""]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":38,"criticalRenown":65,"controversy":28,"llmAffinity":82,"affinityResidual":5.46,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.86,"criticalRenown":0.82,"controversy":0.67,"llmAffinity":0.93},"tags":{"craft":"structural-invention","evidence":"interviews-fieldwork","stance":"moral-seriousness"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"summary":"\"In the early evening of June 25, 1980, Vicki Durian, 26, and Nancy Santomero, 19, were killed in an isolated clearing in Pocahontas County, West Virginia. They were hitchhiking to a festival known as the Rainbow Gathering but never arrived. For thirteen years no one was prosecuted for the \"Rainbow Murders,\" though suspicion was cast on a succession of local men. In 1993, a local farmer was convicted, only to be released when a known serial killer and diagnosed schizophrenic named Joseph Paul Franklin claimed responsibility. With the passage of time, as the truth seemed to slip away, the toll became more inescapable--the unsolved murders were a trauma, experienced on a community scale. Emma Copley Eisenberg spent five years re-investigating these brutal acts, which once captured the national media's imagination, only to fall into obscurity. A one-time New Yorker who took a job in Pocahontas County, Eisenberg shows how a mysterious act of violence against a pair of middle-class outsiders, has loomed over all those involved for generations, shaping their identities, fates, and the stories they tell about themselves.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Murder, west virginia","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-the-third-rainbow-girl-the-long-life-of-a-double-murder-in-appalachia-emma-copley-eisenberg"},{"source":"open_l